`:gt` and `:lt` compare numerically, not lexicographically: id 10 sorts above 3 and is not
below 10, both of which a string comparison would get backwards. Each operator also excludes
the row equal to its operand.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/p3/index.md --
---
id: 3
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/p5/index.md --
---
id: 5
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/p10/index.md --
---
id: 10
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where id:gt=3 --output paths
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where id:lt=10 --output paths
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
plans/p10/index.md
plans/p5/index.md
plans/p3/index.md
plans/p5/index.md
-- stderr --
